  "scope": "S2-53: split public DirectDraw refs from a physical lifetime count including child allocations. DD4/7 explicit surfaces and palettes add one public creator pin; DD1/2 and project DD3 do not. Clippers retain allocation only. Factory wrappers carry creation version; duplicates preserve shared storage/memory and use the project creation profile (Wine duplicate is a partial stub, not a full native oracle). Child destruction unlinks and finishes host/memory work before dropping public/private owner holds. Complex flip roots force-reclaim all implicit children and their allocations even with public refs; implicit zero-count children remain until root. Mip/cube implicit cleanup follows same rule, while soft attachments release their ownership refs. Prevent removal of implicit complex edges; unwind partial flip allocation failure instead of accepting a shortened ring. SetPalette/SetClipper retain replacement before old release. Portable actual C 98967 checks, 160 profiles, 10240 sole-owner same-pointer replacements per binding kind, 32 complex graphs, 32 soft attachments, implicit-zero retention, four allocation failures, storage/memory/final-owner ordering; construction stubs plus actual runtime methods, 18 strict runtime mutations, old actual functions with new versioned helpers runtime control, ASAN/UBSAN. XP real SDK5 creation APIs, public pin deltas,80 same bindings per kind, all public root refs released before upload/alias GPU copy,5 complex roots reclaim10 publicly referenced implicit children. 30 surface objects over25 physical textures,5 palettes,5 clippers,5 readbacks. XP pixel replies are transport controls; independent GPU replay validates320 pixels and all25 explicit physical destructions before5 device destroys. Prior frozen captures still retain their historical implicit leaks; this capture establishes corrected cleanup. Existing shared per-interface COM public count model, implicit initial-count quirks, arbitrary callback/reentrant graph cycles, soft detach/API caps policy, full thread/device-loss/Reset/format/wrapper conversion, S2-54/55/57, native HAL, games/FPS and review stages4/5/6 remain open. D3D8/9 and host/protocol/shader/bundle unchanged.",
